<!--
  BlockML Core — validation semantics branch

  FQN: org.blockml.core.Validation
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.core">

  <idea>How a constraint violation should be reported — separate from the constraint condition itself.</idea>

  <documentation>Abstract branch for validation semantics. A Validation block describes whether and
    how BlockML itself should enforce an attached constraint. Constraints reference Validation via
    the optional validation property on org.blockml.core.Constraint. When validation is omitted,
    the BlockML validator ignores the constraint — it remains metadata for renderers, editors,
    runtimes, and custom validators. Standard implementations live in org.blockml.validation.*;
    domain libraries may define additional Validation blocks (for example
    com.machineblocks.validation.ManufacturingWarning). The BlockML validator only interprets
    Validation types it understands; other tools may interpret additional Validation blocks.</documentation>
  <name>Validation</name>
  <type>core:Validation</type>
  <baseType>core:Block</baseType>
  <abstract />

</block>
